{"name":"Garden Grove","hex":"#5e7f57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Garden Grove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Orange County, California, United States.","A small town in Decatur County, Iowa, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Garden_Grove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden Grove, California","blocks":[{"text":"Garden Grove is a city in northern Orange County, California, United States. The population was 171,949 at the 2020 census. State Route 22, also known as the Garden Grove Freeway, passes through the city in an east–west direction. The western portion of the city is known as West Garden Grove."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Crys-ext.jpg/330px-Crys-ext.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Grove%2C_California","wikidata":"Q50054"},{"title":"Garden Grove, Iowa","blocks":[{"text":"Garden Grove is a small city in Decatur County, Iowa, United States. The population was 174 at the time of the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/GardenGroveTownCenter.JPG/330px-GardenGroveTownCenter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Grove%2C_Iowa","wikidata":"Q1932573"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gar